From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: deepak1556 <hop2deep@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:25:31 +0900
Subject: inspector: avoid JS execution in DOMStorage.getDOMStorageItems

Protocol messages from a remote frontend are dispatched from a V8 API
interrupt, where executing JavaScript is disallowed.

DOMStorageAgent::getDOMStorageItems() previously looked up
globalThis.localStorage and globalThis.sessionStorage via
v8::Object::Get(), invoking their lazy JS getters on globalThis. In
addition, Storage::GetAll() opened the backing store via
Storage::Open(), which threw a JS Error on failure only for the
inspector agent to catch it with v8::TryCatch.

Track live Storage instances in webstorage::BindingData when the
inspector subclasses construct them in Storage::New(), using the flag
they pass to tell localStorage from sessionStorage, since both can be
in memory. Check HasRealNamedCallbackProperty() before reading the
global property so the lazy JS getter is not invoked during an
interrupt. When the store has not yet been initialized by JS
during an interrupt, read the SQLite backing file directly for
localStorage and return an empty map for sessionStorage. Factor
Storage::OpenConnection() to return open errors as a C++ string rather
than throwing a JS exception in Storage::GetAll().

Backported from https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/66740
(upstream commit c43f994f82934bc1b9e516789666ffa430325838).

Co-authored-by: Christian Aurich Zanettini Martins <christian.aurichzm@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: deepak1556 <hop2deep@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Christian Aurich Zanettini Martins <christian.aurichzm@gmail.com>

